scnet-f120.int8.onnx — SCNet (Sparse Compression Network) music source separation, re-instantiated
for a 120-frame (~2.8 s at 44.1 kHz, n_fft 4096, hop 1024) input window so one inference fits a
phone browser's memory. Every learned weight is unchanged from the upstream ONNX; only the
fixed time-axis DFT matrices and the shape constants were regenerated for the shorter window
(scripts/scnet_reframe.py, deterministic).

Upstream ONNX:  https://huggingface.co/audiojs/scnet (revision e71bcdb42bce1d62b7fae25ba90fcbcf90f73f46,
                scnet.int8.onnx, SHA-256 98228931494151762a1c4ab1ec7899a894b1f81fd4a509921a9d2f9bacc50845)
Original model: SCNet (Tong, Zhu, Chen, Kang, Jiang, Li, Wu, Meng, ICASSP 2024, arXiv:2401.13276),
                https://github.com/starrytong/SCNet. Checkpoint as distributed by
                ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training (Roman Solovyev); ONNX export and int8
                compaction by audiojs. Trained on MUSDB18-HQ (Rafii et al., 2019).
License:        MIT. The weights' author confirmed (starrytong/SCNet#35, 2026-07-17) that the
                pretrained weights are MIT and that format-converted versions may be redistributed
